<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108037" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπήν-η</span></b> , ἡ, prop.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hair on the upper lip</i>
			(which is the first to grow, cf. sq.), <i>moustache,</i> distd.
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώγων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				100
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>: generally, <i>beard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ὑ. ἄκουρον τρέφων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					476
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολύνων τὴν ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1286
				</span></i>
			 (troch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκοντες ὑπήνας</span>
			letting the <i>beard</i> grow long, trailing <i>beards,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1072
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ ὑπήνης,</span> of one
				<i>with a huge beard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				122
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				518b18
			</span></i>, it seems to mean <i>the upper lip,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ τὴν ὑ. καὶ τὸ γένειον δασὺ
			ἔχειν,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				20.22
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
